# Docker build context allowlist for the MeepCoin daemon build.
#
# DENY EVERYTHING, THEN NAME WHAT GOES IN. The build context previously included the whole
# repository: results/, .git/, local build trees, attachments, logs, wallets, caches and unrelated
# workspace content were all uploaded to the daemon so that a handful of files could be copied out
# of them. That is a privacy and a correctness problem at once -- it ships things that have no
# business leaving the machine, and it makes the image depend on files nobody declared.
#
# The MeepHash entries below are not a directory glob, and they are two different things:
#
#   4.  EXACTLY the 24 files named in node/daemon-source/MEEPOW_BUILD_INPUTS.json -- the derived
#       meepow_v2/BLAKE3 compile closure plus the one build-selection input. These are the bytes the
#       daemon compiles, and the 013cfbef... aggregate identity covers them and nothing else. Keep
#       this list and that manifest in step; verify_lock.py fails the build if a declared input is
#       absent.
#
#   4b. ONE configure-only source, meepow/src/meepow.cpp. meepow/CMakeLists.txt declares the legacy
#       v1 `meepow` library before its MEEPOW_LIB_ONLY return, so CMake's generate step needs the
#       path to exist, but the requested daemon targets link meepow_v2 and must never compile it.
#       It is NOT part of the 24-file identity: node/docker-build.sh pins its size and SHA-256
#       separately, and fails the build if a legacy object or libmeepow.a appears.
#
# No other MeepHash file can enter the image.

# 1. Deny the entire repository.
*

# 2. The build recipe itself.
!node/Dockerfile
!node/Dockerfile.offline-variant
!node/docker-build.sh

# 3. The daemon source lock: patches, verifier, checksums, manifest.
!node/daemon-source/**

# 4. The locked MeepHash compile inputs, named one by one.
!meepow/CMakeLists.txt
!meepow/include/meepow/meepow.h
!meepow/include/meepow/v2.hpp
!meepow/include/meepow/v2_c.h
!meepow/src/blake3_xof.hpp
!meepow/src/dataset.hpp
!meepow/src/dataset_backend.hpp
!meepow/src/dataset_v2.hpp
!meepow/src/endian.hpp
!meepow/src/epoch.hpp
!meepow/src/meepow_v1.hpp
!meepow/src/meepow_v2.hpp
!meepow/src/params.hpp
!meepow/src/params_v1.hpp
!meepow/src/program.hpp
!meepow/src/target.hpp
!meepow/src/v2_api.cpp
!meepow/src/v2_capi.cpp
!meepow/src/vm.hpp
!meepow/third_party/blake3/blake3.c
!meepow/third_party/blake3/blake3.h
!meepow/third_party/blake3/blake3_dispatch.c
!meepow/third_party/blake3/blake3_impl.h
!meepow/third_party/blake3/blake3_portable.c

# 4b. The one configure-only source: present for CMake generate, pinned separately, never compiled.
!meepow/src/meepow.cpp

# 5. Belt and braces: never send version control, build output or local state, even if a rule above
#    were widened by accident.
.git/
.gitignore
**/build/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
